Subject: [PATCH] pylifecycle: disable Apple system logging with GCC

Apple's os_log_with_type macro relies on Clang-specific builtins.
When cross-compiling CPython for Darwin using GCC, those builtins
are unavailable.

Disable the optional unified logging integration for non-Clang
compilers. Keep existing behavior for Clang builds.

Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/Python/pylifecycle.c b/Python/pylifecycle.c
--- a/Python/pylifecycle.c
+++ b/Python/pylifecycle.c
@@ -45,7 +45,9 @@
 #  include <mach-o/loader.h>
 // The os_log unified logging APIs were introduced in macOS 10.12, iOS 10.0,
 // tvOS 10.0, and watchOS 3.0;
-#  if defined(TARGET_OS_IPHONE) && TARGET_OS_IPHONE
+#  if !defined(__clang__)
+#    define HAS_APPLE_SYSTEM_LOG 0
+#  elif defined(TARGET_OS_IPHONE) && TARGET_OS_IPHONE
 #    define HAS_APPLE_SYSTEM_LOG 1
 #  elif defined(TARGET_OS_OSX) && TARGET_OS_OSX
 #    if defined(MAC_OS_X_VERSION_10_12) && MAC_OS_X_VERSION_MIN_REQUIRED >= MAC_OS_X_VERSION_10_12
